# Pairs with VisibilityMatchesDecision. A leaf that treats "a terminal was
# applied" as "the post-saga value is visible" surfaces an ABORTED saga's
# writes, because an abort terminal is a terminal too. Note this mutation is
# uniform across the fan-out, so AllOrNothing still holds once broadcast
# completes: only the sharpened property catches it.
MODULE: VisibilityMatchesDecisionTerminalPresence
TARGET: VisibilityMatchesDecision
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: treats any applied terminal as post-saga-visible, so an aborted saga's writes surface

--- FIND
ProjectedPrepared(t, k) == terminal[t][k] = "commit"
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: the projection tests only that SOME terminal was applied, losing
\* the distinction between a commit terminal and an abort terminal.
ProjectedPrepared(t, k) == terminal[t][k] # "none"
--- END
